From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pr): highlight container-grammar files using full-file
 contents

Container grammars (PHP, Vue, Svelte, Astro, MDX, ERB) skip per-hunk
highlighting because their nested grammars only activate from the top
of the file; the local git/hg/jj backends restore the spans with a
full-file post-pass. The forge PR path never ran that pass, so PHP and
friends rendered completely unstyled in `tuicr pr <n>`.

`fetch_pr_data` now fetches the old/new contents of container-grammar
files on the background thread via `fetch_file_content` (local blob
first, forge API otherwise; capped at 50 files) and attaches them to the
`FilePatch`. `parse_file_patches` then runs
`enhance_with_full_file_highlight` for those files. A side whose
contents do not match the diff's lines (e.g. the base branch moved) is
dropped instead of painting lines with the wrong spans.

Closes #597
